Gatlin anchored the winning mile medley relay (4 minutes 5.72 seconds) and the 3,200 relay (8:43.53). He was also part of the third-place 400 relay (:45.22).
"Harold has been here before and he knows what to do," said Lane coach Charles McClinton, who coached the Indians to 14 straight city relay titles before having his streak snapped two years ago by Chicago Vocational. "Hopefully, this will signal the rebirth of another long Lane Tech winning streak."
Sophomore Danny Silva also stood out for Lane, joining Gatlin on the 3,200 team.
