MICROSOFT Forza Horizon 3: Playground Games Ralph Fulton talks Xbox One X, 4K and great fan-service
Microsoft has today announced that one of the best games on Xbox One is finally getting enhanced for Xbox One X. Remarkable really, because Playground Games racing game is probably one of the best looking games already, not just on Xbox, but any modern day console. Still, it's set to get a damn sight more remarkable when players download the new, free update for the game, which enables it to run in native 4K (3840×2160) on a console for the very first time. Ahead of the new Xbox One X update, we had time to speak with Playground Games Creative Director Ralph Fulton, a man we've had the pleasure of interviewing once before. On that previous occasion when we had the chance to visit Playground Games studio it became clear that fans of the series were at the heart of everything the studio does and the decisions that make. And this latest enhancement, thanks to the power of the Xbox One X - currently the world's most powerful console - feels like another example of Playground putting fan service first. During our quick chat, Fulton covers everything you need to know about the update, his experience of working with the new Xbox One X ChuckWalla dev kit and also, how the latest update makes Forza Horizon 3 feel (almost) like a brand new game. *** Is it difficult juicing as much power from the Xbox One X when you need to still ensure that the game is stable on Xbox One and Xbox One S? Ralph Fulton: So in the context of Forza Horizon 3 that's not been a problem for us, because the game was built specifically for Xbox One but also Xbox One S. That hasn't been an issue for us because it's already stable, so we've been able to approach the enhancements from the perspective of thinking 'now we have the benefit of this enormous engine - in terms of CPU and GPU performance - what are we going to do with it?
