Although it��s arguable how much difference the new features make we don��t think anyone can say that DICE haven��t excelled themselves with the map design. These are amongst the best the series has ever seen and prove that making interesting maps of such size is a specialist skill in which DICE are uniquely practised.
One of the other focuses of Battlefield 4 is the increased role for naval combat and maps such as Paracel Storm are a great example of this, with its scattering of islands battered by a tropical storm. It��s the sort of experience only Battlefield 4 can offer, but many of the others maps are also cleverly interactive.
The factory lines of Zavod 311 can be switched on to distract enemies and mask footsteps, or the massive steel doors of Operation Locker��s snowy fortress can be slammed shut. One of the capture points on Golmund Railway is actually on a train, which, in our favourite gimmick, can be move up and down the track.
