Self-taught artist Belina Buisson-Wright loved to visit art exhibits at libraries, which gave her the resources to learn to draw and paint.
"I remember seeing another artist's work hung in the library and was completely lost in it and inspired. I hoped that one day my work would hang in a library and inspire someone else to dream," according to her website.
Some of Wright's work will be on display at the Lake Eustis Museum of Art, 1 W. Orange Ave., Eustis.
"Color and Culture" exhibit opens Thursday with a reception from 6 to 8 p.m. at the museum of art.
Her works are strongly influenced by her Haitian and African-American heritage.
The local artist taught school for eight years and while in the classroom she began experimenting with acrylics.
The exhibit runs through Nov. 1.
Admission is free to members and $5 for nonmembers.
Details: 352-483-2900 or lakeeustisartmuseum.org.
Opera @ the Library
Giacomo Puccini's "Turandot," the last of his operas, is this month's Opera @ the Library program. The opera will be shown at 1:45 p.m. Sept. 22 in Room 108B at Cooper Memorial Library, 2525 Oakley Seaver Drive, Clermont.
The story of "Turandot" was adapted from an 18th-century Italian fairy-tale play.
Set in ancient China, the opera tells the story of the beautiful and cruel princess Turandot and her upstart suitor, Calaf, who in order to earn Turandot's hand must answer three riddles correctly or be put to death.
